WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:01.470
(musical sting)

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.060
- All right everybody, I wanna finish up

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.280
with something pretty funny
I found on social media.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.396
This is, "What I'm Liking".

00:00:06.396 --> 00:00:09.330
♪ Intro music ♪

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.240
Just recently, a New York
woman was on a flight

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.242
to Florida when she noticed
a certain unpleasant scent

00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:16.980
wafting in the air.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.170
She wanted to figure out
where is was coming from.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.540
So she put a message on
her phone and airdropped it

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.217
for anyone on the plane to see. Turns out,

00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:27.983
most everyone on board was
asking the same question.

00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:30.300
We have her on the line
right now, watching

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.548
on NBC 4 New York.

00:00:31.548 --> 00:00:33.078
What's up Devin?

00:00:33.078 --> 00:00:35.220
(applause)

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.053
- Hi Kelly!

00:00:36.053 --> 00:00:39.545
- You are hilarious, so tell
us more about what happened.

00:00:39.545 --> 00:00:42.060
- Well, okay, so as soon as I boarded

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.360
the plane and I got to
my seat. It- the dreaded

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.390
smell of farts filled
the air, just the worst.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.977
So I- I typed out a note
on my phone, just saying

00:00:50.977 --> 00:00:52.911
"If you're farting please stop"

00:00:52.911 --> 00:00:56.340
And I sent it out through
Air Drop, just anybody

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.810
who had their phones unlocked could

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.078
receive it so I was just
tapping away, sending it out.

00:01:00.078 --> 00:01:00.911
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:00.911 --> 00:01:02.581
And almost immediately, you could start

00:01:02.581 --> 00:01:04.320
to hear laughter erupt.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.761
I heard people giggling in their seats,

00:01:05.761 --> 00:01:09.110
and so I just kept sending
it out anonymously, because

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.834
my hope, Kelly, was that the culprit would

00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:13.117
receive the message.

00:01:13.117 --> 00:01:14.640
(laughing)

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.610
And then soon after my phone
started vibrating, and I was

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.656
getting Air Drops back!

00:01:18.656 --> 00:01:21.388
So people were laughing,
trying to pinpoint

00:01:21.388 --> 00:01:25.401
who did it, what aisle.
If that's you, cut it out.

00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:29.520
Um, and now also on my
flight there were tablets

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.662
behind the seats that you
could play games with so

00:01:31.662 --> 00:01:34.920
I ended up connecting with
people through the Air Drop

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.900
of, people who wanted to play games.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.320
So, I ended up playing
three games of Battleship

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.189
which, a humble brag, I
won all three of my games.

00:01:43.189 --> 00:01:44.550
(laughter and applause)

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.383
- I love you!

00:01:45.383 --> 00:01:47.354
- This whole thing just
turned into a tablet

00:01:47.354 --> 00:01:49.380
AirDrop party.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.427
- I think that is incredible!
My favorite one was,

00:01:51.427 --> 00:01:52.738
"Bro, it's aisle 16".

00:01:52.738 --> 00:01:54.540
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.670
That's my favorite thing ever. So, you say

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.633
there's a lesson in
your experience, right?

00:01:58.633 --> 00:02:02.006
- Yeah! I would say have
some compassion for your seat

00:02:02.006 --> 00:02:05.024
neighbors. Planes are stuffy as it is, so

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:08.014
if you could go to the
restroom before you board.

00:02:08.014 --> 00:02:10.560
Or just you know, relieve yourself but I-

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.483
I too have compassion,
I know that there's-

00:02:12.483 --> 00:02:15.666
people have IBS or
whatever but it was quite

00:02:15.666 --> 00:02:20.010
unbearable. I was pretty
nauseous, um, and I didn't

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.958
even send this out to be funny. I - I

00:02:21.958 --> 00:02:24.912
genuinely sent it out
to solve the problem.

00:02:24.912 --> 00:02:25.745
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:29.550
Um, but it turned into a
plane bonding experience.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.629
So who knew that millions of other people

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:33.712
have related to this.

00:02:33.712 --> 00:02:35.970
- Oh my god. I just
can't wait for everyone

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.650
to know your face and see you on planes

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.340
in the future. This is incredible.
Thank you so much Devin!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.397
I am loving your post right now!

00:02:43.397 --> 00:02:45.180
(applause)

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.800
And that's not all, our season long

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.840
partner Pilot Pen, makers
of friction the go-to

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.490
erasable pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.380
want to celebrate those who take tough

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.874
situations and turn
them around. So they are

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.904
giving you $1,000, how does that sound?

00:02:56.904 --> 00:02:59.339
(applause)

00:02:59.339 --> 00:03:01.980
- Oh my god! Are you
serious? That's amazing!

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.970
- And also, congratulations
on the Battleship wins!

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.610
That is incredible. Thank you so much to

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.440
all our guests this hour: Julianne Hough,

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.080
Michael Carbonaro, and Danielle Kartes.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.340
Y'all have a great day and if it's not,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.240
try and change it!

